    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required the create AUDIT line to additionally include `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, while keeping existing fields.\n\n`membershipLevel` was already logged, so I added `membershipNumber` to `AuditOwnerCreated.java` (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`). Since `membershipNumber` is a derived value with no getter on the `Owner` entity \u2014 it's computed in `OwnerMapper` as `customerCode + \"-M\" + <2-digit registration year>` \u2014 I replicated that same formula in the audit step so the logged value matches the value the API exposes:\n\n```java\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    String membershipNumber = owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\"\n            + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n    AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} \"\n                    + \"membershipNumber={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n            owner.getMembershipLevel(), membershipNumber);\n}\n```\n\nVerification: the new `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 0 failures. A sample emitted line confirms both fields: `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-08-17 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`.",
